### Acceptance Criteria — Deferred to Increment 2 (Safe Filing)

*(Active when REQ-012, REQ-014, and REQ-010 are delivered. Do not implement in Increment 1.)*

- [ ] *(REQ-010/REQ-012)* A user can **Reject** any document in the inbox. Reject is a **soft delete**: the document moves to a Rejected view and is **retrievable by an admin user within 30 days** of rejection.
- [ ] *(REQ-010/REQ-012)* Rejecting a document requires the user to select a reason from a fixed list (e.g. Sent to wrong practice, Unreadable / corrupt file, Duplicate of existing record, Spam / unsolicited, Other). The Reject confirm button remains disabled until a reason is selected.
- [ ] *(REQ-009)* A rejected document is audited: the reason, acting user ERN, document ERN, and timestamp are stored in the immutable audit trail.
- [ ] *(REQ-010/REQ-012)* An admin user can retrieve a document from the Rejected view within the 30-day window. Retrieval restores the document to the inbox with the original triage metadata intact.
- [ ] *(REQ-010/REQ-012)* The confirm action in the Reject dialogue is disabled until the user has selected a reason; the select field is marked invalid if the user attempts to confirm without a selection.
- [ ] *(REQ-014)* The filing metadata panel includes **Confidentiality** and **Patient Online Visibility** controls inline, accessible during the standard filing workflow. Users do not navigate to a separate settings screen to set these values at time of filing.
- [ ] *(REQ-014 + CLIN-010)* Confidentiality defaults to **Standard access** and Patient Online Visibility defaults to **Not visible to patient** (fail-closed defaults). A visible warning is displayed when either default is changed.
- [ ] *(REQ-010)* The workflow panel includes a Task creation step (④ Task) after the coding step. Task creation is required before a document can reach Complete status where tasks are applicable.
- [ ] *(REQ-012)* The workflow panel includes a File step (② File) allowing the user to assign filing metadata and commit the document to the patient record.

