## Dimension 1: Clinical Safety

### Applicable Guardrails
- **CLIN-002:** Patient Data Audit Trail — immutable audit log created before returning patient data
- **CLIN-007:** Hazard Mitigation Evidence — UI controls must implement HAZ-ID mitigations visibly
- **CLIN-009:** Clinical Safety Logging — log safety-critical events using ERN (not NHS number)
- **CLIN-010:** Error Handling Patient Safety — fail closed; never expose null or ambiguous states

### Hazards Addressed

- **HAZ-DOC-001:** Documents visible to users before appropriate clinical review
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Medium
  - **Risk Level:** High
  - **Source:** Known cross-cutting issue (stated by user)

- **HAZ-DOC-002:** Urgent documents not surfaced or deprioritised in high-volume inbox
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Medium
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-003:** Document accessed by wrong user / without appropriate role
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** Medium

- **HAZ-DOC-004:** Inbox state lost on interruption, leading to document processed twice or missed
  - **Severity:** Medium
  - **Likelihood:** Medium
  - **Risk Level:** Medium

- **HAZ-DOC-027:** *(Deferred — Increment 2, tied to Reject feature)* Document incorrectly rejected — a clinically significant letter is never filed to the patient record; the treating clinician is unaware of its existence
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** Medium
  - **Status:** ⏳ Deferred — active when Reject feature is implemented in Increment 2

- **HAZ-DOC-028:** User navigates to the next document in the queue before completing all required processing steps on the current document — the partially processed document remains unactioned and is not visible as incomplete to the clinical team
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Medium
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-029:** Action completion state is ambiguous across queue contexts — a user believes filing, coding, or task creation was completed as a secondary action in an earlier queue but it was not, and the document advances to Complete with missing clinical information
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** Medium

### Mitigations

- **MIT-DOC-001:** Binary urgency indicator (red arrow) surfaced to the left of each document row at triage level; queue supports sorting/filtering by urgent status
  - **Type:** UI Control
  - **Effectiveness:** Partial (accuracy of source urgency flag determines completeness)

- **MIT-DOC-002:** Role-based access control enforced at inbox level; documents only visible to authorised users
  - **Type:** Business Logic + Auth
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-003:** Autosave on all in-progress work; resume state preserved on interruption
  - **Type:** Business Logic
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-027:** *(Deferred — Increment 2)* Reject action requires mandatory reason selection; confirmation step before status applied; action is reversible by admin within 30 days; full audit trail records reason, user ERN, document ERN, and timestamp
  - **Type:** UI Control + Business Logic
  - **Effectiveness:** Partial
  - **Status:** ⏳ Deferred — active when Reject feature is implemented in Increment 2

- **MIT-DOC-028:** "Next document" action is only available after all required workflow steps for the current document are confirmed complete; documents with incomplete required steps remain in-queue and retain a visible in-progress indicator in the queue list
  - **Type:** Business Logic + UI Control
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-029:** The completion state of each action (filed / coded / tasks complete) is displayed prominently and persistently on the document view in all queue contexts; individual action panels are clearly labelled as complete or incomplete; a document cannot reach Complete status if any required action is unconfirmed
  - **Type:** UI Control + Business Logic
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

