## Dimension 2: Information Governance

### Applicable Guardrails
- **IG-001:** Data Minimisation — inbox metadata view returns only fields required for triage
- **IG-002:** Privacy by Design and Default — minimum data surfaced at inbox level; full document requires explicit open action
- **IG-003:** Lawful Basis Declaration — Article 6(1)(e) (public task) + Article 9(2)(h) (health data, medical purposes)
- **IG-004:** Special Category Data Protection — patient health documents are special category data; AES-256-GCM encryption at rest required
- **IG-010:** Retention Policy Enforcement — documents subject to NHS records retention schedules (IF3005)

### Data Handling
- Triage metadata fields (Urgency, Title, Type, Date, Source, Department) are surfaced at inbox list level
- Full document content requires deliberate open action (not surfaced passively in list view)
- Patient identity not exposed at inbox list level beyond what is operationally necessary for triage
- All document access logged (see CLIN-002)

### GDPR Articles
- **Article 6(1)(e):** Lawful basis — public task (NHS direct care)
- **Article 9(2)(h):** Special category health data — medical diagnosis/treatment purposes
- **Article 5(1)(c):** Data minimisation — inbox list view limited to minimum triage fields

---

## Dimension 3: Security

### Applicable Guardrails
- **AUTH-004:** Authorization Required — all inbox endpoints require valid JWT with correct scope
- **SEC-001:** TLS Encryption — all traffic over TLS 1.2+
- **SEC-002:** No Secrets in Code — all credentials/keys in Azure Key Vault

### Security Requirements
- Role-based access: admin and clinician roles may have differentiated inbox views/capabilities
- Session continuity: autosave state must not persist sensitive document content in insecure client storage (e.g. unencrypted localStorage/sessionStorage)
- No patient document content exposed in URL parameters or browser history

