### Accessibility Requirements (WCAG 2.1 AA)

**Compliance Checklist:**
- [x] Perceivable: urgency conveyed by icon + `aria-label`, not colour alone; text contrast ≥4.5:1
- [x] Operable: all rows keyboard-navigable (Tab → row → Enter); ⋮ reachable by Tab; modal focus-trapped
- [x] Understandable: every input has `aria-label`; loading states use `aria-live`; error messages inline + actionable
- [x] Robust: `jest-axe ^9.0.0` in devDependencies; no native `<button>` or `<input>` outside `@emisgroup/ui-*`

**Mandatory Rule A — all inputs labelled:**
```tsx
<Input aria-label={t('inbox.search.ariaLabel')} clearable ... />
<Button ariaLabel={t('inbox.actions.menu', { title: doc.title })} circular ...>
  <Icon ... />
</Button>
```

**Mandatory Rule B — loading and error states announced:**
```tsx
// Loading
<Skeleton.Area role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-label={t('inbox.loading')} />
// Error
<div role="alert" aria-live="assertive">{t('inbox.error.loadFailed')}</div>
// Empty (polite)
<div role="status" aria-live="polite">{t('inbox.empty.allDone')}</div>
```

**Mandatory Rule C — `jest-axe` test pattern:**
```tsx
it('inbox has no accessibility violations', async () => {
  const { container } = render(<InboxScreen />);
  expect(await axe(container)).toHaveNoViolations();
});
```

**Screen reader — urgency:**
```tsx
// Urgent row: icon with label
<Icon aria-label={t('inbox.urgency.urgent')} ... />
// Non-urgent row: visually hidden text so row still conveys urgency state
<span className="sr-only">{t('inbox.urgency.routine')}</span>
```

