### Failure Modes & Resilience

1. Dependency timeout or unavailable: Circuit breaker and bounded retries with explicit fail-closed UX.
2. Message duplication or replay: Idempotency keys and dedupe checks at persistence boundaries.
3. Partial write risk: Transactional outbox or compensating action with audit evidence.
4. EMIS Web downstream outage: Queue and replay integration calls with no silent data loss.

### Integration Points

**Phase 1 — EMIS Web MS SQL (per-domain, read-only via anti-corruption layer):**

| Legacy SP / View | Purpose | Key Inputs | Key Outputs |
|---|---|---|---|
| `InboundDocuments.GetTasks` | Matched document queue (all tabs except Unmatched) | `@UserInRoleId`, `@TaskGroupId`, `@Page`, `@PageSize`, `@SortColumn`, `@SortAscending`, `@GlobalView`, `@FilterTypeId` | Task + patient + document + observation records (paginated) |
| `InboundDocuments.GetUnmatchedTasks` | Unmatched queue (TaskTypeId 803) | `@UserInRoleId`, `@TaskGroupId`, `@Page`, `@PageSize`, `@SortColumn`, `@SortAscending` | Task + document rows, no patient link |
| `InboundDocuments.DocumentTaskStatusDetail` | Status rollup per document | `OrganisationId`, `DocumentGuid` | `PatientMatchingStatus`, `FilingStatus`, `OverAllStatus`, `OverdueActions`, `AssignedActions` |
| `UserTasks.Document` | Link document records to user tasks for Outstanding Tasks view | `DocumentGuid` | Related user task identifiers |
| `UserTasks.UserTask` | Outstanding user task details and status | Related user task identifiers | Task title/type/status/due/assignee fields |
| `WorkflowManager.fnSelectAllTasksforUser` | Resolve visible task set for user (including deputies) | `ModuleId`, `TaskGroupId`, `GlobalUserInRoleId`, `OrganisationId`, `GlobalView`, `ShowTasksForDeputies` | TaskId set |
| `Admin.LocalUserInRoleGlobalMap` | Resolve `UserInRoleId → GlobalUserInRoleId + OrganisationId` | `LocalUserInRoleId` | `GlobalUserInRoleId`, `OrganisationId` |

**Existing modernisation dependency:** A separate User Tasks microservice writes and maintains user tasks in the existing EMIS Web DB (`UserTasks.UserTask` and linkage in `UserTasks.Document`). Documents Manager must consume this as the source of truth for Outstanding Tasks related to a document.

**Per-domain connection resolution:** Service Registry (EMIS Web) → per-domain SQL endpoint → MS SQL connection string. Each of ~100 patching domain databases is queried independently. The new service layer constructs a domain-specific connection based on the authenticated user's organisation context.

**Phase 2 (post-cutover):** EMIS Web DB reads replaced by native Aurora PostgreSQL 17 queries with equivalent indexed access patterns.

**Existing API baseline (openapi-docs.yml):** Endpoints `GET /persons/{personGUID}/documents`, `POST /persons/{personGUID}/document`, `GET /documents/presignedurl`, `GET /persons/{personGUID}/documents/{documentGUID}/metadata`, `GET /persons/{personGUID}/documents/{documentGUID}/file`, `GET /documents/{documentGUID}/temporary-file` are accepted as-is. V1c will add inbox-specific endpoints (`GET /documents/inbox/tasks`, `GET /documents/inbox/unmatched-tasks`) as extensions.

